WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:27.840
Stop.

2
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.960
Unclip.

3
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.960
Go on.

4
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.840
Stop! If I told you to jump.
what would you do? Jump?

5
00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.720
We're looking for people
who can think. not sheep.

6
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.440
It's over for you.

7
00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.960
Okay. you can send the next one.

8
00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:52.920
Villiers!

9
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:55.960
Next up. Villiers.

10
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:27.680
Alright. you can go.

11
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.560
Go on.

12
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.480
Stop. Look at me.

13
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.800
Raise your arms.

14
00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.480
Unclip yourself.

15
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.040
No.

16
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:07.160
"No"? Are you afraid of taking risks?

17
00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.000
I don't take unnecessary risks.

18
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.600
Alright. you can go to the end.

19
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.320
Stop! Raise your knee.

20
00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.600
Now sing.

21
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.560
Sing!

22
00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.960
The blue sky above us could collapse

23
00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.480
I can't hear anything! Can you?

24
00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.320
And the Earth might as well crumble

25
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.520
I don't care. as long as you love me

26
00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:59.480
I couldn't care less
About the rest of the world

27
00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.120
As long as love fills my mornings

28
00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.320
Stop.

29
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.040
What's with the sappy song?

30
00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.040
I'm a hopeless romantic. Major.

31
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.960
Alright. you can come back.

32
00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.360
Wait.

33
00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.400
Why are you here?

34
00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.680
To join the GIGN Tactical Force.

35
00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.760
Why?

36
00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.240
It's the most effective tactical force--

37
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:33.200
Stop with your recruitment bullshit.
Why are you here. Max?

38
00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.800
Because I can be the best.

39
00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.360
Better than your father?

40
00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.200
What makes you think
that you have what it takes?

41
00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.600
The truth is. I don't know.

42
00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.520
It's the only thing I want.
I'll do anything to prove myself.

43
00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.400
Next. Lemoine.

44
00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.480
What do they ask you on the beam?

45
00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.680
Just some bullshit to throw you off.

46
00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.360
You were right to push him.

47
00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.960
You don't want people to think
you're favoring your godson.

48
00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.880
You did the right thing.

49
00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:30.000
ELITE FORCE

50
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.400
NATIONAL GENDARMERIE
GIGN

51
00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.520
Come on. guys. That's weak.

52
00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:39.960
Come on.

53
00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.200
Shooters. when you're ready.
start the count.

54
00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.080
Shooter one. ready.

55
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.880
Shooter two. ready.

56
00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.840
HOSTAGES FREED IN DARING GIGN OPERATION

57
00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:02.520
Three. two. one.

58
00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.480
KOUACHI
THE FINAL ASSAULT

59
00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.440
Thirteen.

60
00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.280
Fourteen.

61
00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:18.200
Fifteen.

62
00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.920
CAUTION
ELECTRIC FENCE

63
00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:23.760
Hey.

64
00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:30.960
France Info.

65
00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.320
General Paloméros will be our guest with--

66
00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.240
Where are you?

67
00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.360
I'm coming! I'm here.

68
00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:40.480
That looks cute.

69
00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.520
Is it new?

70
00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.440
-This?
-Yeah.

71
00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:46.200
Yeah. do you like it?

72
00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.200
Yeah. it's nice.

73
00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:50.720
Do you have the matching bottoms?

74
00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.080
Take a guess.

75
00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:53.640
Show me.

76
00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.440
No. I don't think I will.

77
00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:56.760
-Come on. show me.
-No.

78
00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.160
I'll show you when you resign
and move back to Paris.

79
00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.520
I'm waiting until recruitment's over.

80
00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:04.600
Hi. sweetheart.

81
00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.000
Go ahead. help yourself.

82
00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:09.040
Like you'd say no.

83
00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.040
Hi. sweetheart.

84
00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.800
Forget it. she's gone.
She doesn't care. she's 16.

85
00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.760
Not even a hi for her dad.

86
00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.000
I'll see her tonight.
I'll come straight to the conservatory.

87
00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:21.960
That was yesterday.

88
00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.640
-You're messing with me.
-I'm not.

89
00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.920
Her rehearsal has always been on the 5th.

90
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.280
Fuck.

91
00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:31.400
I was sure it was tonight.

92
00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:32.920
How was it?

93
00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:36.280
ALERT 1

94
00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.960
I love you. I have to go. I'll call you.

95
00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.000
Go.

96
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.600
This is the army's weapons depot
in Châteaudun.

97
00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.040
Four soldiers shot dead.

98
00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.120
I can see that.

99
00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.080
Two other soldiers are missing.
They may have been taken hostage.

100
00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.880
It happened fast. Very violent.

101
00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:05.040
-Kalash. Kalash. and an Uzi?
-Yeah. an Uzi.

102
00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.800
It's clear the terrorists
know the site very well.

103
00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:10.520
They destroyed several of the cameras.

104
00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.200
They move precisely. They stay calm.

105
00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.440
These guys are pros.

106
00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.680
We're looking for clues to identify them.

107
00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:20.000
They're used to working together.
They could be mercenaries.

108
00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.960
But why take such a big risk for weapons?
You can get them anywhere.

109
00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.960
This is a bit unusual.
Those pallets contain explosives.

110
00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.840
CL20. a compound
still under military testing.

111
00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.480
-That's what they stole.
-It'd just been delivered.

112
00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.560
It's the most powerful explosive known.

113
00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.960
One ton of it.

114
00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.600
-Do we know where they are?
-Not yet.

115
00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:43.800
Intel are on it. We just got the footage.
They'll find them.

116
00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.480
I reassigned Tanya to your section.

117
00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:47.960
Stop the truck and retrieve the cargo.

118
00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.440
You're in command.

119
00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:50.680
You're not coming?

120
00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:53.080
The men don't need me. I'm staying at HQ.

121
00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.280
Wait. there's a camera
they didn't take out.

122
00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:57.400
Let's see.

123
00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.760
Look. there. On the roof.

124
00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:02.160
-A cooling unit.
-Yeah.

125
00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:03.720
That means it has a GPS chip.

126
00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.320
We'll check with the investigators
and track it down.

127
00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.600
Your section is on the ground.

128
00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:11.320
-You're the helicopter gunner.
-Okay.

129
00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.360
A Caracal just arrived from Villacoublay.

130
00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.600
-We'll stick with 82.
-Very well.

131
00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.600
Chloé. keep us posted
on that refrigerator truck.

132
00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:19.960
Will do.

133
00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.680
COMMIT FOR LIFE
NATIONAL GENDARMERIE

134
00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:38.800
-Start the battery.
-Battery.

135
00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.560
I'll handle the radios.

136
00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.040
-Stick recentered. Checklist completed.
-Roger.

137
00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:09.440
Okay. go.

138
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.600
Take vehicle four.

139
00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.520
Hey. Tanya.
Glad to have you with us. Miss Explosive.

140
00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.800
-You good?
-Yeah. you?

141
00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.280
-Priority to Tactical.
-Mustache. respect your elders.

142
00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:27.400
Get in the other car.

143
00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:29.880
Don't forget. I can blow your balls off.

144
00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.120
Valère's tiny little balls!

145
00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.720
Come with me.

146
00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.040
Nice car.

147
00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.480
Yeah. it was seized in a drug run
at the Spanish border last week.

148
00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.520
They're leaving!

149
00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.280
Shouldn't we finish up?

150
00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.720
Mop the floor if you want.
we're going to watch.

151
00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:02.640
AIR AND SPACE FORCE

152
00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:03.640
Let's go.

153
00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:06.880
We'll expand.

154
00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.760
-Sit down.
-General.

155
00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.120
Vertical climb. increasing power.

156
00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.640
We've got him.
The GPS shows him on a back road

157
00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.120
heading towards Chartres. 40 km away.

158
00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:26.160
Everyone head for the A10.

159
00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.560
There may be two hostages.

160
00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.200
What are you doing?

161
00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:34.720
Villiers. Colonel.

162
00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:37.520
We heard about the op.
We came to show our support.

163
00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.520
Stand in the corner. Not a peep.

164
00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.840
Invisible. Understood?

165
00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.080
Visual on target.

166
00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.080
Kilometer 81. he's heading south.

167
00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:17.960
Target alone. No other vehicles.

168
00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.880
He's driving fast.

169
00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.520
There's a town 1.5 km ahead.

170
00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.280
There's also a school
at the town entrance.

171
00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.200
That could be a target.

172
00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.960
It's transporting one ton of CL20.

173
00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:47.600
It could wipe out the entire area.

174
00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:48.960
I'll stop them before that.

175
00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.720
If it flips over.
it could explode and take you with it.

176
00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.160
If you have a better idea. I'm all ears.

177
00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:57.120
Otherwise. you know what you have to do.

178
00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.640
Everyone. move back.

179
00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:01.720
Cédric. stay back and move in afterward.

180
00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.680
Alright. we'll keep our distance.

181
00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:10.240
Move across to the left!

182
00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.000
The school is 1 km ahead.

183
00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.160
There's a school bus approaching.

184
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.080
They'll cross paths in 800 meters.

185
00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.360
The driver is alone in the cab.

186
00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:32.080
Target immobilized.

187
00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.720
Right next to the bus.
There are a lot of kids.

188
00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:36.880
Shit!

189
00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:40.640
I'm going down.

190
00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:42.200
No. I'm the negotiator.

191
00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.480
Negative. take care of the bus.

192
00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.600
The bus is blocked.
There's nothing I can do. I'm stuck!

193
00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:06.200
Look. they're lowering a rope.

194
00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.000
Gendarmerie. put your hands up!

195
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.240
Put your hands up!

196
00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.160
There he is. He's coming.

197
00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.640
I want to see your hands above your head!

198
00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:49.880
Raise both hands
above your head right now!

199
00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:53.960
Put your hands up!

200
00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.800
I'm not armed. They forced me.

201
00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.320
I had no choice.

202
00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.880
They forced me. I swear.

203
00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.680
I have to blow myself up.

204
00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:10.760
It's too late now.

205
00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:15.280
Raise your hands above your head.
fingers interlocked.

206
00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:17.160
Team Alpha in position.

207
00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:19.240
Open up!

208
00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:24.480
Hello. children. Everything is fine.
We're going to get off the bus together.

209
00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:27.320
My wife and kids are at home.

210
00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:30.280
They'll kill them
if I don't deliver this shipment.

211
00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:31.840
Raise your hands up. now.

212
00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:33.680
Bus evacuation underway.

213
00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:35.840
Second team approaching.

214
00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:37.560
Both hands. Your other hand.

215
00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.120
My name is Sergeant Osman.

216
00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:40.640
I'll check.

217
00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:44.600
Move forward. Try to stay calm.

218
00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:47.880
Ma'am. take a few of the kids
and we'll get off the bus calmly.

219
00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.520
It's my family or me. I have no choice.

220
00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:53.720
Raise your left hand.
I need to see what's in your left hand!

221
00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:02.400
Fuck.

222
00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:05.120
He has a release trigger.

223
00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.760
-Please.
-Come on. that's good.

224
00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:08.880
Cédric. move it.
It could go off any minute.

225
00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.280
-Come on. guys.
-Let's go.

226
00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.960
Tanya. any updates?

227
00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:15.480
There are crates. I'll inspect the door.

228
00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:18.960
Osman is one of the soldiers
who disappeared from the base.

229
00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:20.680
-Okay.
-He may be a hostage.

230
00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.720
Okay. Sergeant Osman. is that it?

231
00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:25.000
-Yes.
-We're sending a team to find his family.

232
00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.760
Everything's fine.

233
00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:29.680
Go help the others with the kids.

234
00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:32.600
Sergeant Osman. look.
I'm putting my weapon away.

235
00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.160
Okay.

236
00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.240
-I'm scared.
-Keep moving.

237
00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.000
Keep running. don't stop.

238
00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.000
Will they shoot?

239
00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.320
Don't stop.

240
00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:50.480
Door check okay. opening now.

241
00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:55.920
I'm getting in.

242
00:17:58.240 --> 00:17:59.880
Look at me.

243
00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:01.440
Everything's fine.

244
00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:04.440
Look at me. Stay with me. please.

245
00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.440
I'm going to slowly approach your door

246
00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:09.160
and open it so we can talk. Is that okay?

247
00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:11.360
I'm opening the door.

248
00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:15.120
Look at me.

249
00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.000
Look at me. Do you have kids?

250
00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:19.560
Sarah and Nora.

251
00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.240
Sarah and Nora are lovely names.

252
00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:23.400
They're at home.

253
00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:26.040
I know. What we're doing here with you.

254
00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:28.720
we're also doing for your family at home.

255
00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:32.320
Bus evacuated. The children are safe.

256
00:18:34.640 --> 00:18:38.160
No parallel circuit.
Everything's connected to the trigger.

257
00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:41.920
Look at me.

258
00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.640
I want you to think about your daughters.

259
00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.480
The more you think about them.
the harder you squeeze. okay?

260
00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.880
Alright.

261
00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:51.040
Squeeze your left hand.

262
00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:53.120
-Squeeze it. very hard.
-Okay.

263
00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:58.120
David. I need his trigger
in order to disarm the system.

264
00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:00.920
About 60 CL20 tubes are connected.

265
00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:06.400
You can lower your right hand.

266
00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:10.160
That's it. Great. look at me.

267
00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:15.320
Now. reach out your left hand.
Very slowly.

268
00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:18.040
Reach out your left hand.
Look at me. Osman.

269
00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:21.840
I can't do anything. I need the detonator.

270
00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.880
Look at me. Osman.
Think about your daughters.

271
00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:29.480
That's great. Keep going.

272
00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.640
You're doing great.

273
00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:34.720
Look at me. Osman.

274
00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.920
Fantastic. That's it.

275
00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:40.840
Everything's fine.

276
00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:43.480
Everything's fine.

277
00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.320
We can free you from this now.

278
00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.600
It's almost over.

279
00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.160
Well done. Sergeant.

280
00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:59.000
NATIONAL GENDARMERIE
GIGN

281
00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:03.680
We found Osman's family
unharmed at their home.

282
00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.440
Tied up and gagged.

283
00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:07.800
The hostage takers had left a while ago.

284
00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:10.600
The sergeant didn't know.
so he kept following orders.

285
00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:14.800
His mission was to drop off the cargo
in an abandoned parking lot near Chartres.

286
00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:17.440
He was ordered to blow himself up
if we intercepted him.

287
00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:18.960
We stopped him.

288
00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.240
At the meeting point.
we found a second refrigerator truck

289
00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:24.040
that we hadn't seen on the cameras.

290
00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.760
Inside. a driver.

291
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.640
The second soldier taken hostage.

292
00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.160
Shot dead.

293
00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.240
He was given the same orders as Osman.

294
00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:33.440
They threatened to kill his family too.

295
00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:35.920
They killed him
when he delivered the cargo.

296
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.520
We didn't find anything
in the back of the truck.

297
00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.320
But he was definitely
transporting stolen CL20.

298
00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.800
Their operation was sophisticated.
professional even.

299
00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:47.600
It was deliberate
and had been planned long ago.

300
00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:49.360
Tanya. go ahead.

301
00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:54.600
CL20 is a cutting-edge explosive.

302
00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:57.640
Originally. it was a failed pesticide
made in the USA.

303
00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:00.240
-Can you start the video. please?
-Yeah.

304
00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:04.080
This is the DGA's testing base.

305
00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:05.760
A test from five years ago.

306
00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:08.600
That was just 2 kilos.

307
00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.160
It's the most powerful
conventional explosive.

308
00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:14.240
Extremely difficult to handle.

309
00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:16.480
Less than ten people
in Europe are trained in it.

310
00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:20.040
The last time I saw it was in Afghanistan.
An American stock.

311
00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:23.080
France has never publicly admitted
to synthesizing it.

312
00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:25.320
Yet that's what was stolen last night.

313
00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:28.600
One ton. And only half of it
was in the van we intercepted.

314
00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.480
-So 500 kilos are still out there.
-Yes.

315
00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:33.680
Versailles SR
and the DGSI are on the case.

316
00:21:33.760 --> 00:21:36.440
Intelligence and Reconnaissance
are at their disposal.

317
00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:38.920
Christophe. will you brief the FI?

318
00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:40.760
Yes. General. I'll take care of it.

319
00:21:41.880 --> 00:21:43.400
Okay. guys. Let's go.

320
00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:45.040
-Eat?
-Yeah.

321
00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:46.320
Let's go.

322
00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:52.200
It takes balls
to hit a weapons depot like that.

323
00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:54.120
They're audacious.

324
00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:56.000
We'll never hear the end of it.

325
00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:57.400
I won't be here anymore.

326
00:21:57.920 --> 00:21:59.760
Hello. Houston. anybody there?

327
00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:02.360
When did we last talk?

328
00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:05.640
-We're talking now.
-No. really talk.

329
00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:09.480
Yesterday you showed me
that awful motorbike you want to--

330
00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:10.440
David.

331
00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:13.440
What's wrong?

332
00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:16.560
Pancreatic cancer. Stage three.
That's what's wrong.

333
00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:20.320
The doctor says I have 5 to 6 months left.

334
00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:22.440
Maybe seven. I'm a stubborn bastard.

335
00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:24.600
But it's over.

336
00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:27.080
It's over?

337
00:22:28.960 --> 00:22:32.160
What do you mean? "It's over"?
You talk like that?

338
00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:33.800
You got this far talking like that?

339
00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:36.920
There are some battles
you can't prepare for.

340
00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:38.400
We're not trained for this.

341
00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:41.960
I won't win this fight. It's over.

342
00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:43.440
So. I'm quitting.

343
00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:46.080
I want time with my family.

344
00:22:47.400 --> 00:22:49.240
You've neglected yours too.

345
00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:51.360
Yeah.

346
00:22:51.440 --> 00:22:52.280
David.

347
00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:55.720
Don't feel guilty about leaving.

348
00:22:55.800 --> 00:22:57.840
It's the right decision for you and Jess.

349
00:22:57.920 --> 00:23:00.040
-Yeah.
-She's been waiting for too long.

350
00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:02.520
You had the best missions.

351
00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:05.000
I'll spare you Max's file.

352
00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:07.520
You can't stay if he graduates.

353
00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:10.840
You know very well he won't graduate.

354
00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:20.440
Always a joy dining with you.

355
00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:22.280
Is there anyone in this place?

356
00:24:33.400 --> 00:24:34.480
Where's Manon?

357
00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:36.040
She went to the gym.

358
00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:38.080
-That's good.
-Yeah.

359
00:24:45.800 --> 00:24:47.000
Thanks.

360
00:24:52.160 --> 00:24:54.080
I can't believe it about Christophe.

361
00:24:54.800 --> 00:24:55.840
It's tough.

362
00:24:56.600 --> 00:24:59.120
Has it made you
reconsider your resignation?

363
00:24:59.840 --> 00:25:01.520
No. quite the opposite.

364
00:25:02.280 --> 00:25:03.840
I've made up my mind.

365
00:25:04.600 --> 00:25:06.920
We have to make our dream come true.

366
00:25:08.360 --> 00:25:10.360
A sailing trip around the world.

367
00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:12.680
I'll announce it
at the graduation ceremony.

368
00:25:12.760 --> 00:25:14.040
I want to do things right.

369
00:25:14.800 --> 00:25:16.720
And Max? He's about to graduate.

370
00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:19.560
-You're going to leave him all alone?
-No. but…

371
00:25:22.040 --> 00:25:24.200
There's no way Max will graduate.

372
00:25:26.760 --> 00:25:28.480
Max won't graduate.

373
00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:30.840
So?

374
00:25:31.560 --> 00:25:33.760
Ready for the trip of a lifetime?

375
00:25:33.840 --> 00:25:36.560
Shit. Mom. actually.
my class is at 9:00 a.m.

376
00:25:36.640 --> 00:25:38.120
-Dad?
-Hey.

377
00:25:38.200 --> 00:25:39.680
I didn't know you were here.

378
00:25:44.080 --> 00:25:46.520
-What?
-You guys are acting weird.

379
00:25:46.600 --> 00:25:49.520
-No. you're acting weird.
-Yeah. super weird.

380
00:25:49.600 --> 00:25:52.360
-Yeah.
-Yeah. that must be it. Okay.

381
00:25:52.440 --> 00:25:53.880
Mom. can you drive me. please?

382
00:25:53.960 --> 00:25:55.080
No. I'm going to work.

383
00:25:55.160 --> 00:25:57.160
It'll take four hours on the subway.

384
00:25:57.240 --> 00:25:59.040
Go get your helmet. I'll take you.

385
00:25:59.760 --> 00:26:00.600
Are you sure?

386
00:26:01.800 --> 00:26:04.720
What? Can't I take my daughter
to her piano lesson?

387
00:26:04.800 --> 00:26:06.800
-Go get your helmet.
-I'll get changed.

388
00:26:06.880 --> 00:26:08.960
-Okay.
-Wow. this is a first.

389
00:26:16.600 --> 00:26:18.360
I love you.

390
00:26:19.360 --> 00:26:22.160
It's 8:42 a.m.
The 17th district is 6 minutes away.

391
00:26:22.240 --> 00:26:23.920
-Plenty of time.
-What? The 17th?

392
00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:28.200
You know. I'll be able to take you
to the conservatory more often.

393
00:26:28.280 --> 00:26:31.720
And spend more time with you
if you're not too embarrassed.

394
00:26:31.800 --> 00:26:33.680
-We'll spend more time together.
-But…

395
00:26:34.600 --> 00:26:37.080
Great. but Dad.
it's no longer in the 17th.

396
00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:40.080
My new conservatory is in Saclay.

397
00:26:40.160 --> 00:26:41.520
-Saclay?
-Yes.

398
00:26:42.760 --> 00:26:44.120
Okay. we'll be on time.

399
00:26:44.200 --> 00:26:46.600
-Hold on tight.
-We won't be on time. Crap.

400
00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:53.240
What is this. Club Med? You're not cold?

401
00:26:53.320 --> 00:26:54.720
No!

402
00:26:54.800 --> 00:26:57.000
That's bullshit. even I'm cold.

403
00:26:57.080 --> 00:26:58.560
You're not cold?

404
00:26:58.640 --> 00:27:00.520
Yeah. to be honest. we're freezing.

405
00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:03.000
You only had to say.
We're not assholes here.

406
00:27:03.080 --> 00:27:05.160
We'll give you some gear to warm up.

407
00:27:05.240 --> 00:27:06.680
Some nice heaters.

408
00:27:07.840 --> 00:27:11.600
Here. are you cold?
Come on. Raise your arms.

409
00:27:12.880 --> 00:27:14.640
-It warms you up. huh?
-It sure does.

410
00:27:14.720 --> 00:27:16.280
Pass it to your buddy.

411
00:27:17.120 --> 00:27:18.600
And with a smile. guys.

412
00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:23.240
Be careful with that one.
it's the General's. so…

413
00:27:24.720 --> 00:27:25.880
Better not put it down.

414
00:27:25.960 --> 00:27:29.160
Three. two. one. go.

415
00:27:31.400 --> 00:27:34.480
Joining the GIGN
puts you among the top tier.

416
00:27:34.560 --> 00:27:38.400
The elite of all tactical forces.
But it doesn't come easy!

417
00:27:41.280 --> 00:27:42.440
If I go into battle.

418
00:27:43.160 --> 00:27:46.440
I need to know that I can put my life

419
00:27:47.160 --> 00:27:49.360
in my squadmates' hands.

420
00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:56.000
If you want to be part of it.

421
00:27:56.080 --> 00:28:00.480
we have to be absolutely certain
that we can do the same with you.

422
00:28:00.560 --> 00:28:03.880
Come on. I'll add a little atmosphere.
It's a smoke bomb.

423
00:28:05.480 --> 00:28:06.600
Don't stop. come on!

424
00:28:08.080 --> 00:28:09.640
Come on!

425
00:28:10.240 --> 00:28:11.880
I see some of you shaking.

426
00:28:11.960 --> 00:28:14.440
If you're tired. you can put it down.

427
00:28:16.080 --> 00:28:17.240
I'm sorry.

428
00:28:17.920 --> 00:28:19.760
You can try again next year.

429
00:28:21.080 --> 00:28:22.080
100 meters away.

430
00:28:22.160 --> 00:28:25.480
At 100 meters.
one click equals one centimeter.

431
00:28:25.560 --> 00:28:28.800
I want to see you put five bullets
right between the eyes.

432
00:28:29.440 --> 00:28:30.640
Good luck. gentlemen.

433
00:28:39.360 --> 00:28:41.560
Two weeks ago. there were 100 of you.

434
00:28:41.640 --> 00:28:44.160
How many of you are here tonight?
Fourteen.

435
00:28:44.240 --> 00:28:45.920
It's the end of recruitment.

436
00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:49.600
If you don't have what it takes.
let me make it clear. we don't care.

437
00:28:50.800 --> 00:28:52.280
We won't take on any of you.

438
00:28:52.360 --> 00:28:53.360
None.

439
00:28:59.280 --> 00:29:02.080
On the other hand.
for those of you who are still here

440
00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:03.600
at the end of this process.

441
00:29:03.680 --> 00:29:05.600
you'll have earned your spot.

442
00:29:06.400 --> 00:29:08.800
Don't forget you're doing this
for under 2000 bucks.

443
00:29:09.320 --> 00:29:11.160
If you want to give up. now's the time.

444
00:29:26.120 --> 00:29:27.440
Still not eliminated?

445
00:29:28.760 --> 00:29:30.040
Still haven't given up?

446
00:29:32.960 --> 00:29:34.520
Come on. keep pushing. ma'am.

447
00:29:36.360 --> 00:29:38.880
Congratulations. it's a boy.

448
00:29:39.400 --> 00:29:42.760
If you're lucky enough to join my section.

449
00:29:43.920 --> 00:29:47.520
and Cédric's.
then we will give our lives for you too.

450
00:29:48.480 --> 00:29:50.920
But in the meantime. arms outstretched!

451
00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:05.440
We're going to change the next test.

452
00:30:06.360 --> 00:30:07.440
Defusing.

453
00:30:08.040 --> 00:30:11.680
It's odd to change it at the last minute.
We don't deal with explosives.

454
00:30:11.760 --> 00:30:14.760
Cédric. we dealt
with explosives yesterday.

455
00:30:15.760 --> 00:30:17.400
It can happen.

456
00:30:18.520 --> 00:30:20.720
We have to adapt
and be ready for anything.

457
00:30:22.200 --> 00:30:24.160
-Is this because of Max?
-Yeah.

458
00:30:24.760 --> 00:30:27.680
Don't be such an ass. David.
You do know what this means to him?

459
00:30:27.760 --> 00:30:30.480
We're on a mission. there's a bomb.
and he freezes. What then?

460
00:30:30.560 --> 00:30:33.720
Stop. This isn't to test him.
It's to make him screw up.

461
00:30:35.640 --> 00:30:37.640
You're scared
he'll end up like his father.

462
00:30:48.120 --> 00:30:50.520
Djibril. we're changing the last exercise.

463
00:30:50.600 --> 00:30:53.760
Stop everything. guys.
We're changing exercises.

464
00:31:06.640 --> 00:31:07.480
Look at me.

465
00:31:19.600 --> 00:31:20.560
Come on. buddy.

466
00:31:57.600 --> 00:31:59.480
Tanya to Max. do you copy?

467
00:32:01.560 --> 00:32:02.800
Loud and clear.

468
00:32:02.880 --> 00:32:05.640
Catch your breath. Breathe.

469
00:32:08.760 --> 00:32:11.200
That's it. Now move forward.

470
00:32:13.080 --> 00:32:14.480
-And observe.
-Hey.

471
00:32:53.120 --> 00:32:54.160
There's a wire.

472
00:33:05.280 --> 00:33:06.920
It goes toward the stairs.

473
00:33:07.440 --> 00:33:08.840
It goes toward…

474
00:33:11.960 --> 00:33:13.600
It goes toward an electric panel.

475
00:33:15.760 --> 00:33:16.760
It's…

476
00:33:16.840 --> 00:33:18.280
Shit. I triggered something.

477
00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:20.920
Well done. You have one minute.

478
00:33:43.840 --> 00:33:46.040
I see an improvised explosive device.

479
00:33:47.400 --> 00:33:48.600
A tube. some wires.

480
00:33:49.200 --> 00:33:50.800
Okay. I know which one to cut.

481
00:34:28.040 --> 00:34:29.080
Disarmed.

482
00:34:48.120 --> 00:34:48.960
Congratulations!

483
00:34:49.040 --> 00:34:51.640
Yeah. come on. make some noise!

484
00:34:52.240 --> 00:34:53.320
Congratulations!

485
00:34:54.640 --> 00:34:55.520
She said yes!

486
00:34:56.120 --> 00:34:58.800
I'm getting married. guys!

487
00:34:58.880 --> 00:35:00.520
Congratulations!

488
00:35:18.880 --> 00:35:21.160
-Yeah.
-It's going to be a great ceremony.

489
00:35:21.240 --> 00:35:22.800
-Great start.
-Yeah.

490
00:35:22.880 --> 00:35:25.680
-General.
-Hello. Jess. If you'll excuse me.

491
00:35:26.200 --> 00:35:27.440
How are you?

492
00:35:32.280 --> 00:35:33.840
Thanks for your message.

493
00:35:36.160 --> 00:35:38.200
-It's the big night. huh?
-Yeah.

494
00:35:38.280 --> 00:35:39.360
Have you seen David?

495
00:35:39.440 --> 00:35:40.440
No. I haven't.

496
00:36:14.040 --> 00:36:15.320
It's been a while.

497
00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:17.000
Fifteen years.

498
00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:24.640
You promised he'd never be admitted.

499
00:36:25.320 --> 00:36:26.760
Nathalie.

500
00:36:27.480 --> 00:36:31.800
I did everything I could.
I even sabotaged all his tests.

501
00:36:32.280 --> 00:36:35.400
I was much harder on him than anyone else.

502
00:36:36.280 --> 00:36:38.160
What do you want me to do? Max is…

503
00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:41.200
He's talented.

504
00:36:47.080 --> 00:36:49.120
Talent doesn't stop you getting killed.

505
00:36:53.200 --> 00:36:54.640
If I lose him too…

506
00:36:55.360 --> 00:36:56.920
This fucking place…

507
00:36:57.880 --> 00:36:59.480
It took Laurent from me.

508
00:37:01.840 --> 00:37:03.600
Now it's taking my son.

509
00:37:05.760 --> 00:37:07.040
Promise me

510
00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:09.640
that you'll protect him.

511
00:37:09.720 --> 00:37:12.080
That you'll never leave Max on his own.

512
00:37:12.760 --> 00:37:13.960
Do you hear me?

513
00:37:14.920 --> 00:37:16.160
Never.

514
00:37:18.120 --> 00:37:21.200
Don't forget that it's because of you

515
00:37:21.280 --> 00:37:23.120
that I lost my husband.

516
00:37:54.800 --> 00:37:56.120
Pierre-Jean Lemoine.

517
00:37:56.640 --> 00:37:59.080
Tactical Force. section one.

518
00:38:07.080 --> 00:38:08.640
Wear it with dignity and pride.

519
00:38:10.840 --> 00:38:12.160
Well done. PJ!

520
00:38:12.760 --> 00:38:14.400
Groom to be!

521
00:38:14.480 --> 00:38:16.000
NATIONAL GENDARMERIE INTERVENTION GROUP

522
00:38:21.760 --> 00:38:24.960
Raphaëlle Ricci.
Intelligence and Reconnaissance Force.

523
00:38:35.040 --> 00:38:37.120
Wear it with dignity and pride.

524
00:38:38.760 --> 00:38:39.920
Well done. Rapha!

525
00:38:40.680 --> 00:38:42.360
You're the best!

526
00:38:42.960 --> 00:38:43.920
Well done!

527
00:38:46.360 --> 00:38:47.200
You earned it!

528
00:38:52.800 --> 00:38:56.440
Maxime Villiers.
Tactical Force. section one.

529
00:39:21.680 --> 00:39:23.240
Wear it with dignity and pride.

530
00:39:25.120 --> 00:39:26.240
Well done. Max!

531
00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:36.960
Well done!

532
00:39:38.920 --> 00:39:41.320
I believe you wanted to add something?

533
00:39:41.400 --> 00:39:43.840
-Yeah. David!
-Davido!

534
00:39:51.040 --> 00:39:55.360
Sorry. I'm not very good at speeches.

535
00:39:58.480 --> 00:40:02.880
Today is a special day. Very special.

536
00:40:03.800 --> 00:40:05.360
For you as well as for me.

537
00:40:06.560 --> 00:40:10.040
Because after a brutal selection process.

538
00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:12.240
you are now part of the group.

539
00:40:14.600 --> 00:40:15.560
Congratulations.

540
00:40:15.640 --> 00:40:20.240
It's an exceptional group
that you will be living with.

541
00:40:21.040 --> 00:40:24.360
It's a bit like a family.
A demanding family.

542
00:40:27.120 --> 00:40:28.800
One that will demand sacrifices.

543
00:40:29.720 --> 00:40:34.120
And you'll only be able
to make those sacrifices

544
00:40:35.160 --> 00:40:38.520
if you have the support of your families.

545
00:40:40.240 --> 00:40:41.960
However. your families…

546
00:40:43.120 --> 00:40:45.560
didn't choose this.
They're subject to it.

547
00:40:46.720 --> 00:40:48.160
So. thank you.

548
00:40:49.520 --> 00:40:50.960
Thank you because

549
00:40:52.560 --> 00:40:56.560
you are the ones
who have to show the most courage.

550
00:40:57.760 --> 00:41:02.960
You have to put up with
the constant delays.

551
00:41:03.040 --> 00:41:04.520
The beepers going off.

552
00:41:04.600 --> 00:41:07.680
The fear in your gut
when they go on a mission that's

553
00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:10.040
difficult.

554
00:41:10.120 --> 00:41:11.920
Then there's the distance.

555
00:41:12.440 --> 00:41:14.680
At the end of the day.
maybe the true heroes

556
00:41:15.520 --> 00:41:16.640
are your families.

557
00:41:18.520 --> 00:41:19.960
Let's get the party started.

558
00:41:20.520 --> 00:41:22.160
See you in the field tomorrow.

559
00:41:25.480 --> 00:41:27.840
-Thank you!
-Yeah. David!

560
00:41:27.920 --> 00:41:29.120
Bravo!

561
00:42:19.280 --> 00:42:21.360
Thanks for everything you've done.

562
00:42:21.440 --> 00:42:23.960
-Of course. You've earned your place.
-Thanks.

563
00:42:28.880 --> 00:42:31.400
David. where are you going? Come back.

564
00:42:55.800 --> 00:42:57.360
I can't leave Max.

565
00:43:00.120 --> 00:43:01.160
I can't.

566
00:43:08.560 --> 00:43:10.440
I was offered a position at the bank.

567
00:43:12.440 --> 00:43:15.000
It's a huge promotion.

568
00:43:17.520 --> 00:43:18.840
That's great.

569
00:43:21.680 --> 00:43:23.040
But it's in Singapore.

570
00:43:26.440 --> 00:43:28.440
I didn't tell you about it because

571
00:43:29.360 --> 00:43:30.800
there was no point.

572
00:43:31.960 --> 00:43:34.760
I knew you wouldn't give it all up
to come with me. and…

573
00:43:37.280 --> 00:43:40.960
For me. the most important thing
has always been our family.

574
00:43:44.680 --> 00:43:46.680
But obviously. it's different for you.

575
00:43:49.280 --> 00:43:51.080
Manon and I don't come first.

576
00:43:51.160 --> 00:43:53.120
You do. but…

577
00:43:54.120 --> 00:43:55.160
Jess…

578
00:43:57.040 --> 00:43:58.240
And Max?

579
00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:02.160
Will you tell him
why you're doing all this?

580
00:44:09.040 --> 00:44:11.200
Give me some time. please.

581
00:44:16.200 --> 00:44:17.200
As for Singapore.

582
00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:18.840
I'm going to say yes.

583
00:44:26.480 --> 00:44:27.920
I'll head back to Paris now.

584
00:44:45.400 --> 00:44:47.280
Why the Tactical Force?

585
00:44:47.360 --> 00:44:50.440
Sure. they're the best of the best. but…

586
00:44:51.120 --> 00:44:53.280
I mean. what's the real reason?

587
00:44:53.920 --> 00:44:56.600
David and my father
were in the same section.

588
00:44:57.080 --> 00:44:58.920
They were like brothers. and…

589
00:45:00.120 --> 00:45:02.320
One day. an op went wrong.

590
00:45:03.880 --> 00:45:05.040
The explosion?

591
00:45:05.640 --> 00:45:06.600
Yeah.

592
00:45:06.680 --> 00:45:08.600
Fifteen years ago.
after my father's death.

593
00:45:08.680 --> 00:45:11.320
my mother wanted us
as far away from the GIGN as possible.

594
00:45:12.520 --> 00:45:14.200
I only came back this year.

595
00:45:16.080 --> 00:45:19.440
But my real home has always been here.

596
00:45:20.640 --> 00:45:21.840
In Satory.

597
00:45:22.640 --> 00:45:24.120
In Tactical. like my father.

598
00:45:31.240 --> 00:45:32.280
And you. Intel?

599
00:45:32.800 --> 00:45:35.360
Intelligence and Reconnaissance.
Was that your goal?

600
00:45:36.680 --> 00:45:39.160
Why are you being condescending
all of a sudden?

601
00:45:40.640 --> 00:45:44.840
Intelligence and Reconnaissance
was my dream. you know?

602
00:45:45.400 --> 00:45:46.520
It's my calling.

603
00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:48.800
Plus. I'm good at it.

604
00:45:49.760 --> 00:45:51.760
Tracking down guys. following leads…

605
00:45:55.680 --> 00:45:57.320
Honestly. I don't get you. David.

606
00:45:59.680 --> 00:46:01.960
At least remove Max
from your section. damn it!

607
00:46:04.480 --> 00:46:05.800
I forgave you.

608
00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:08.440
But does he know what really happened?

609
00:46:09.400 --> 00:46:10.280
No.

610
00:46:25.760 --> 00:46:28.360
How are you gonna handle
having him with you in the field?

611
00:46:29.640 --> 00:46:30.640
How?

612
00:46:37.600 --> 00:46:39.840
You think you're staying for him.
You're delusional.

613
00:46:49.120 --> 00:46:50.240
You're kidding yourself.

614
00:52:28.320 --> 00:52:33.320
Subtitle translation by: Alison Simpson
